Precedence (higher number = tighter binding)

120 : Postfix call / index / field           (call_suffix)
110 : Prefix unary                            (!, - , +)
100 : Multiplicative                          (*, /, %)
90  : Additive                                (+, -)
80  : Shift                                   (<<, >>)
70  : Comparison                              (<, >, <=, >=)
60  : Equality                                (==, !=)
50  : Bitwise AND                             (&)
45  : Bitwise XOR                             (^)
40  : Bitwise OR                              (|)
35  : Logical AND                             (&&)
30  : Logical OR                              (||)
25  : Conditional (ternary)                   (?:)  -- right-associative
20  : Assignment                              (=, +=, -=, etc.) right-assoc
10  : Comma / low binding                      , (argument separator)
This table informs Pratt parselet binding powers.

3) Parser Architecture (design doc)
Save as crates/x3-parser/README.md or add to OpenSpec.

Key goals

Deterministic parsing (no ambiguous constructs).

Good error messages and recovery (for dev UX).

Produce canonical AST nodes matching crates/x3-ast.

Support for plugin-ish builtin macros and foreign-call constructs.

Efficient single-pass parse with O(n) complexity.

Modules

crates/x3-parser/
  ├─ src/
  │   ├─ lib.rs            -- re-exports parser API
  │   ├─ grammar.rs        -- grammar constants + token names
  │   ├─ error.rs          -- ParseError, diagnostics
  │   ├─ tokens.rs         -- TokenStream wrapper (thin)
  │   ├─ parser.rs         -- Pratt / statement parsing
  │   └─ tests/            -- unit tests + fixtures
Core components

TokenStream — deterministic iterator over lexer tokens; provides peek(n) and consume().

Parser — owns a TokenStream, provides parse_program().

Pratt expression engine:

Prefix parselets: for literals, identifiers, unary ops, grouped (.

Infix parselets: for binary ops, call/index/field (postfix handled as infix with high precedence).

Use binding powers driven by the above operator table.

Statement parsers: top-level parse_item(), parse_stmt(), parse_block(), and specialized parse_atomic_block(), parse_agent_block() etc.

Deterministic diagnostics: always sort multi-element errors and include deterministic token positions.

Error recovery

On error in block body, skip tokens until semicolon or a new top-level } or ; to resume.

Provide suggestions (expected ;, expected ), missing identifier) using error.rs.

Integration

compiler::compile_program will call x3_parser::parse_program(src) -> Result<ast::Program, ParseError>.

Determinism

All parser outputs must be canonical: e.g., lists preserved left-to-right, maps use Vec of pairs not HashMap.

